error[E0422]: `Reading` doesn't implement `Key`
  --> tests/programs/interfaces/eq_key/not_key.la:6:13
  |
6 |     let m = #{Reading { at: 1, value: 0.5 }: 1};
  |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = help: add `with Key` after `Reading`'s declaration, or implement it by hand with `impl Key for Reading`

error[E0451]: `f64` can't be a key: it is a float
  --> tests/programs/interfaces/eq_key/not_key.la:7:12
  |
7 |     let s: Set<f64> = #{};
  |            ^^^^^^^^
  |
  = help: floats compare with `==` but aren't `Key`: `NaN != NaN`, so a float key could never be found again; use an integer

error[E0451]: `f64` can't be a key: it is a float
  --> tests/programs/interfaces/eq_key/not_key.la:7:23
  |
7 |     let s: Set<f64> = #{};
  |                       ^^^
  |
  = help: floats compare with `==` but aren't `Key`: `NaN != NaN`, so a float key could never be found again; use an integer

For more about E0422 and E0451, run `lughac explain <code>`.
